{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
Oh, give me a [G]home where the buffalo [C]roam,
Where the [G]deer and the antelope [D]play,
Where [G]seldom is heard a dis[C]couraging word,
And the [G]skies are not [D]cloudy all [G]day.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[D]Home, home on the [G]range,
Where the deer and the antelope [D]play,
Where [G]seldom is heard a dis[C]couraging word,
And the [G]skies are not [D]cloudy all [G]day.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
How often at [G]night when the heavens are [C]bright
With the [G]light from the glittering [D]stars,
Have I [G]stood here amazed and [C]asked as I gazed
If their [G]glory ex[D]ceeds that of [G]ours.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 3"}
Where the air is so [G]pure, the zephyrs so [C]free,
The [G]breezes so balmy and [D]light,
That I [G]would not exchange my [C]home on the range
For [G]all of the [D]cities so [G]bright.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
{x_end: G}
